{"check":{"claim":"The mpeg_card.bin image Yabause hands to the Saturn BIOS through the Get MPEG ROM command (0xE2) changes what the BIOS shows and does for a Video CD.","method":"Experimental build, not what RetroArch users run: libretro Yabause with yinit.mpegpath pointed at the system directory, which reaches the same cs2.c Cs2GetMPEGRom path that standalone Yabause uses when its MpegROM/Path setting is filled. Saturn BIOS v1.01 (Japan), one emulation thread, host clock frozen at 2000-01-01 00:00:00 by libfaketime 0.9.10 so runs are deterministic, the authored Video CD inserted. 3000 frames; the button the core maps to Saturn A held 15 frames from frame 1300 (Play on the BIOS CD player) and Start 15 frames from frame 1900. Repeated with each mpeg_card.bin image, with no file, with 512 KiB of zeros and with a 1-byte file; every other input is identical. Each variant runs twice in fresh processes.","observable":"video_sha1","result":{"groups":[{"value":"c89177305da310bd329a17d0f4a5e60ffe5cdece","variants":["mpeg_card.bin","mpeg_card.bin.3fee63d4","mpeg_card.bin.80179c49","mpeg_card.bin.821af2bd","mpeg_card.bin.b60e8866","mpeg_card.bin.b7450812","mpeg_card.bin.ee821d3f","mpeg_card.bin.ef9de845","mpeg_card.bin-absent","zeros_512k.bin","one_byte.bin"]}],"statement":"video_sha1 is identical across all 11 variants","status":"same"},"variable":"mpeg_card.bin"},"core":{"build_command":"make -j8 in yabause/src/libretro, after setting yinit.mpegpath to <system>/mpeg_card.bin in libretro.c (the port sets it to NULL)","commit":"8926b0c6c347f8c5c755911ddb0ac695420ffbf8","compiler":["GCC: (Ubuntu 13.3.0-6ubuntu2~24.04.1) 13.3.0"],"file":"yabause_libretro.so","library_name":"Yabause","library_version":"v0.9.15 625bee35c","repo":"https://github.com/libretro/yabause","sha256":"1530b0a3c7f2ff762e4b02e22f016be6753a7f3864306cf17ca810bccee0e5c4"},"data":{"bytes":2962,"sha256":"e746187f0118ee5f4ed90458021bb36c215b723f7ef36198fb25d1e40e008fe5"},"emulator":"yabause","flags":[],"frontend"